{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And when you sell.</b> In any sale there must be no form of deception, as the Sages said (Bava Metzi'a 60a): he must not sweep [dust] over the mouth of the measure, for this is nothing but stealing the eye." "<b>Or acquire.</b> When the seller does not know the true value of the thing, even though it was already in his possession and he had time to show it to a merchant or to a relative." "<b>You shall not deceive.</b> Even though they said there is no claim of deception for land (Bava Metzi'a 56a), nevertheless [the prohibition applies here]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:54.911994697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}